    blogOnlineDot: {
      title: 'How to show a bot as online without the green dot',
      pill: 'Behind the scenes',
      h1: 'How to show a bot as online without the green dot',
      author: 'Liam',
      date: 'October 24, 2026',
      bannerAlt: 'A bot listed as online without the green dot',
      lede: 'Some Discord bots, like appeal.gg, are listed with the online members but have no green dot and no status. We wanted our feedback bot to look like that, and after a lot of trying we found an order of steps that works. This is what we did, what did not work, and what we are not sure about.',
      h2_1: 'What we wanted',
      p1: 'Our feedback bot (feed) publishes the posts of the feedback board in the Petto server. It does not need to read messages, so it can talk to Discord only over HTTP, and an HTTP-only bot does not have the green dot or the status bubble. The problem was that Discord listed it under "Offline", which looks like it is broken.',
      h2_2: 'What Discord says (and does not say)',
      list2: [
        ['A bot that only uses HTTP has no status', ': the status (online, idle, do not disturb) is sent through the gateway, the connection that keeps a bot online. With no gateway, no dot.'],
        ['There is a mark for these bots', ': the bot user can carry the public flag BOT_HTTP_INTERACTIONS, documented as "Bot uses only HTTP interactions and is shown in the online member list". Discord sets it, not the bot.'],
        ['What Discord does not say', ': when it sets the mark, or why a bot that has it can still be listed as offline. We did not find it written anywhere.'],
      ],
      h2_3: 'What did not work',
      list3: [
        ['Only setting the Interactions Endpoint URL', ': the bot got the mark (we checked it with the API) and was still listed as offline.'],
        ['A role that shows its members separately', ': an offline member never goes into a role group.'],
        ['A brand new application', ': it behaved the same when we looked at it a few minutes later.'],
        ['Waiting', ': it did not change on its own.'],
      ],
      h2_4: 'What worked, step by step',
      steps: [
        'Have the application with its bot user, its token and its public key (Developer Portal, General Information).',
        'Run the bot connected to the gateway first, so it shows with the green dot.',
        'Make a small web server that answers Discord\'s PING at /interactions and checks the Ed25519 signature of every call with the public key. Discord only saves the address if this works.',
        'In the Developer Portal, set the Interactions Endpoint URL to that address and save it.',
        'With the URL already saved, turn the gateway off and restart the bot (in feed this is the variable FEEDBACK_GATEWAY=off). The bot keeps posting and answering buttons over HTTP.',
        'Wait a few minutes, close Discord and open it again. The bot is listed with the online members, with no dot and no status.',
      ],
      h2_5: 'Why we think it works (this is a guess)',
      p5: 'Another application of ours ended up listed this way after it disconnected from the gateway while it already had the URL saved, even though nothing was answering its interactions. The one that disconnected before the URL existed stayed offline. So our guess is that the order matters: the disconnection has to happen when the application already has the Interactions Endpoint URL. It worked for us, but Discord has not documented it and it can change.',
      h2_6: 'What to keep in mind',
      list6: [
        ['It is only for bots that do not need the gateway', ': a bot that reads messages or direct messages needs it, and then it shows its normal status.'],
        ['Buttons and slash commands work', ': they arrive as signed calls to your address, and the bot answers within three seconds (or answers first and finishes after).'],
        ['If you take the URL away', ', the buttons go back to the gateway. The bot can handle both, so it is safe to switch.'],
      ],
      h2_7: 'Credits',
      p7: 'This was found by Liam, who tried every step on real servers, sent the screenshots and noticed what the other application was doing. Claude, his research assistant, helped with the research, the tests and the corrections.',
    },
    blogCurrentlyLog: {
      title: "Introducing the Currently log: every change of Petto, in color",
      pill: "Product",
      h1: "Introducing the Currently log: every change of Petto, in color",
      author: "Liam",
      date: "November 15, 2026",
      bannerAlt: "Cards in the colors of the Currently log: red, yellow, green, blue, orange, purple, gray and black",
      lede: "Petto now has a Currently log: one channel where every change is posted the moment it goes live, like the releases of a GitHub project, with a color for each kind of change, a short explanation and a picture.",
      h2_1: "What it is",
      p1: "Until now, what changed in Petto was spread over the changelog, the wiki and the announcements. The Currently log puts the changes of each version in one place. When Petto starts with something new, it posts it in the channel, once, in English. Each post says what changed, where it belongs and how it affects you, links the documentation when there is some, and shows up to three pictures. Every post comes with a like and a dislike, so you can tell us what you think.",
      h2_2: "The colors",
      list2: [["Red", ": a security fix, or something important for your safety."], ["Yellow", ": a new feature, like a whole new group of commands."], ["Green", ": something added to a feature that already exists: a variable, a command or an option."], ["Blue", ": an improvement, or a change in how something behaves."], ["Orange", ": a fix."], ["Purple", ": the web, the dashboard, the docs and the blog."], ["Gray", ": a command, a variable or an option that was removed from a feature."], ["Black", ": a feature that was removed completely."]],
      h2_3: "How a post looks",
      p3: "Changes of the same kind go together in one card, five at a time, and each one keeps its own pictures. The most important kinds come first.",
      shots: [["/assets/log/currently-log-colors-1.png", "Cards of the Currently log in red, yellow, green and blue"], ["/assets/log/currently-log-colors-2.png", "Cards of the Currently log in orange, purple, gray and black"]],
      h2_4: "How it works",
      list4: [["Written once", ": the changes of a version are written in a file with their kind, the area they belong to, the explanation, the link and the pictures."], ["Posted at the start", ": when Petto starts, it posts the ones it has not posted yet and remembers them, so a restart never repeats a post."], ["In English", ": it is the language of the bot, so the log reads the same for everybody."], ["Real pictures", ": they are made with the same code the bot runs, so what you see is what Petto answers."]],
      h2_5: "What is in the first one",
      list5: [["Partner top lists", ": three new variables show the five best managers of the day, the week and all time."], ["17 new variables", ": the top lists, ten about the server (age, emojis, stickers, vanity link, rules channel, verification level...) and four about a member (roles, top role, owner, days in the server)."], ["/purge in every channel", ": an option to clean the whole server, with a list of what it would delete and a confirmation button first."], ["/mhistory", ": the cases a moderator has given."], ["Fixes", ": the icons of a case, /forum used outside a post, and /guildtag and /vanity in the menu."]],
      shots5: [["/assets/log/partner-top-lists.png", "A partner message with the top lists of the week and of all time"], ["/assets/log/new-variables.png", "A message that uses the new server and member variables"], ["/assets/log/purge-all-channels.png", "The confirmation of /purge in every channel"], ["/assets/log/mhistory.png", "The answer of /mhistory"], ["/assets/log/case-detail.png", "The card of a case with the hammer icon"]],
      h2_6: "Where to read it",
      p6: "The Currently log lives in the Petto support server. If you only want the big picture of a version, the changelog of this site still has each release with its notices.",
    },
